<%# My games: every match this identity holds a seat in, newest first (TASK-BRIEF 1.7).

    Identity is a signed-in user or the guest key in this browser's cookie, decided by the
    controller; a match that was only looked at is not here. Everything a row shows comes from
    the three queries the controller ran, so this page touches the database not at all. %>
<% content_for :title, "My games" %>

<h1>My games</h1>

<% if @matches.empty? %>
  <p class="lede">
    <% if Current.user %>
      Nothing here yet. Games you play signed in as
      <%= Current.user.display_name %> are listed on this page, and so are any you started as a
      guest in this browser before you signed in.
    <% else %>
      Nothing here yet. Games you start in this browser are listed on this page, even without
      an account, and they become yours for good if you sign up.
    <% end %>
  </p>
  <div class="button-row">
    <%= link_to "Start a game", root_path, class: "button" %>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <p class="lede">
    <%= pluralize(@matches.length, "match") %>, newest first. Every game is saved: open one to
    carry on where it stopped, or replay a finished one move by move.
  </p>

  <%# A guest is identified by a cookie in this browser and nothing else, so this list is
      the browser's, not a person's: a cleared or expired cookie leaves the games in the
      database and at their addresses but takes them off this page for good (session-7 audit,
      finding L8). Say so, once, where it matters, and only to a visitor it applies to. %>
  <% unless Current.user %>
    <p class="games__note">
      These games belong to this browser, not to an account: clearing this browser's cookies
      loses sight of them. <%= link_to "Sign up", new_registration_path %> or
      <%= link_to "sign in", new_session_path %> and they become your account's for good.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <%# The explicit roles are not decoration. Below 40rem history.css gives every part of this
      table `display: block` so five columns become one stacked card per game and the page
      never scrolls sideways at a 360 px viewport; in Chromium and Firefox a display change
      like that takes the table semantics out of the accessibility tree with it, and these
      roles put them back. The column name each cell loses when the header row is hidden is
      carried in data-label and printed by CSS in front of the value. %>
  <table class="games" role="table">
    <caption class="games__caption">Your matches, newest first</caption>
    <thead role="rowgroup">
      <tr role="row">
        <th role="columnheader" scope="col">Game</th>
        <th role="columnheader" scope="col">Opponent</th>
        <th role="columnheader" scope="col">State</th>
        <th role="columnheader" scope="col">Moves</th>
        <th role="columnheader" scope="col">History</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody role="rowgroup">
      <% @matches.each do |match| %>
        <tr id="match-row-<%= match.id %>" class="games__row" role="row">
          <th role="rowheader" scope="row" class="games__mode">
            <%= link_to mode_label(match), match_path(match), class: "games__link" %>
            <span class="games__when"><%= match.created_at.to_fs(:long) %></span>
          </th>
          <td role="cell" class="games__opponent" data-label="Opponent"><%= opponent_name(match, @seats_by_match[match.id]) %></td>
          <td role="cell" class="games__state" data-label="State"><%= state_sentence(match) %></td>
          <td role="cell" class="games__count" data-label="Moves"><%= pluralize(@move_counts.fetch(match.id, 0), "move") %></td>
          <td role="cell" class="games__history" data-label="History">
            <%# The replay and the export are offered on finished games, which are the ones
                there is a whole game to read. Both exist for every match (an unfinished
                replay opens at the start, an unfinished export ends in *), and the match page
                is one click away for a game still in play. %>
            <% if match.finished? %>
              <%= link_to "Replay", match_replay_path(match), class: "games__link" %>
              <%= link_to "Export PDN", match_path(match, format: :pdn), class: "games__link" %>
            <% else %>
              <%= link_to "Open", match_path(match), class: "games__link" %>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>
